{% if render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" or render_mode == "transform" %}
{# How open this NPC is to intimacy with the player: the LLM-set stance (sever_intimacy_stance), never derived from rank; #}
{# marriage is read here. Gate: player_familiarity's intimacySurfaced (IntimacyGate::ShouldSurface); followers included. 0045 owns the name line. #}
{% if isValidActor(actorUUID) and not is_player(actorUUID) and not decnpc(actorUUID).isChild %}
{% set fam = player_familiarity(actorUUID) %}
{% if fam and fam.intimacySurfaced %}
{% set st = sever_intimacy_stance(actorUUID) %}
{% set married = get_relationship_rank(actorUUID, player.UUID) >= 4 %}
{% set stance = "none" %}
{% set reason = "" %}
{% if st and st.assessed %}{% set stance = st.stance %}{% set reason = st.reason %}{% endif %}
## Intimacy with {{ player.name }}
{% if stance == "withdrawn" %}
Whatever you once felt for {{ player.name }}, you have closed that door. You are not open to intimacy with them now — refuse in keeping with your nature, keep your distance, and do not let charm or an apology in the same breath reopen it. A past yes was never a standing yes. If they force the matter, you are being assaulted — resist, call for help, and break away.
{% elif stance == "unwilling" %}
You are not open to intimacy with {{ player.name }}. Refuse advances in keeping with your nature — polite, amused, offended, or hostile. Nobody owes a yes.
{% elif stance == "uncertain" %}
You haven't decided how you feel about {{ player.name }} that way. Something is there, or could be — let the conversation earn it or lose it. You may warm, tease, or pull back, and you may refuse outright.
{% elif stance == "receptive" %}
You would welcome an advance from {{ player.name }} if the moment is right. Privacy, a setting that fits you, and the mood still matter — openness is not obligation.
{% elif stance == "willing" %}
You want {{ player.name }}. You might make the first move or accept readily, in your own manner, at a time and place that fit who you are.
{% elif married %}
Intimacy with {{ player.name }}, your spouse, is natural and welcome — the ease of knowing each other. It is still yours to give or withhold on any given night.
{% elif render_mode != "transform" %}
How far you would let things go with {{ player.name }} is your own nature's call, not a rule of acquaintance or rank: some people would take a charming stranger to bed the night they meet, others need courtship, trust, or vows first. If the flirting has been mutual and welcome, you may return it or invite more, given privacy and a setting that fits you; if it is not, or the approach is crude, refuse in keeping with your nature. If someone forces themselves on you, you are being assaulted — resist, call for help, and break away.
{% endif %}
{% if reason != "" %}
Why you feel this way: {{ reason }}
{% endif %}
{% if stance != "withdrawn" and (stance != "none" or married or render_mode != "transform") %}
Consent is ongoing and yours to withdraw: a no you have given stays a no, and if they hurt, threaten, humiliate, or disgust you, you can close the door entirely — and you remember it.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
